invariant: INV-26
file: quic.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh
reason: a QUIC host object's session seals its Initial packets as though
  its caller had set CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, whatever ch_cfg.cpu says,
  so a session on a CPU without the AES instructions runs them on its
  first packet and dies of SIGILL. Both ciphers compute the same packet,
  so every loop passes on a CPU with the instructions, and
  bin/aes_runtime_test, which counts the calls into aes_hw.c, links no
  quic.c. test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh runs the handshakes without the bit on
  a CPU model without AES-NI or PCLMULQDQ. The lane skips without docker,
  and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    int rc = QUIC_INITIAL_SEAL(q->t.cfg.cpu, CH_QUIC_SELF(q), version, q->initial_dcid,
--- new
    int rc = QUIC_INITIAL_SEAL(CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, CH_QUIC_SELF(q), version, q->initial_dcid,
